  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.1. Increased capacity of Member States to formulate and implement national employment policies in response to the COVID-19 crisis</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">By October 2023, ILO Constituents in Lebanon adopted an integrated action plan towards formalization of the informal economy. The validation of the diagnostic on the informal economy, focused on the agriculture, agribusiness, and construction sectors and was completed during last quarter of 2023. Further to the ILO&apos;s informality and vulnerability study conducted in Lebanon, as well as the policy brief, an informality diagnostic was undertaken as part of a more comprehensive employment and labour market diagnostic in Lebanon. 
The diagnostic was conducted through its SOLIFEM Project &quot;&quot;Social Dialogue for Formalization and Employability in the Southern Neighbourhood Region&quot;&quot;. For this diagnostic, ILO has partnered with the Ministry of Labour, the Association of Lebanese Industrialists (ALI), the General Confederation for Lebanese workers (CGTL), and the National Federation for Workers and Employees Trade Unions in Lebanon (FENASOL). This diagnostic focused on informality in three target sectors where recommendations formed the basis for the development of an action plan on formalization, and which will be closely aligned with the development of the first national employment policy for Lebanon, as well as the ILO&apos;s efforts in relation to social protection.</narrative>
   </description>
